{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q414989","formula":"ThSiO₄","hill":"O4SiTh","elements":["O","Si","Th"],"composition":{"O":4.0,"Si":1.0,"Th":1.0},"names":{"en":"Thorite","ru":"Торит","uk":"Торит"},"descriptions":{"en":"Thorite, (Th,U)SiO4, is a rare nesosilicate of thorium that crystallizes in the tetragonal system and is isomorphous with zircon and hafnon. It is the most common mineral of thorium and is nearly always strongly radioactive. Thorite was discovered in 1828 on the island of Løvøya, Norway, by the vicar and mineralogist, Hans Morten Thrane Esmark.","ru":"Тори́т — силикат тория, минерал тетрагональной системы, дитетрагонально-бипирамидального класса. Химическая формула торита — ThSiO4, но он всегда содержит множество посторонних примесей. Изоморфен с рутилом, цирконом, касситеритом.","uk":"Торит — мінерал класу силікатів, ортосилікат торію острівної будови."},"fame":31,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q12089225","names":{"en":"mineral species","ru":"действительный вид минералов","uk":"мінеральний вид"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-5836","atoms":47,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[7.142,0.0,0.0],[0.0,7.142,0.0],[0.0,0.0,6.336]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":3.168,"el":"Th"},{"x":0.0,"y":7.142,"z":3.168,"el":"Th"},{"x":7.142,"y":0.0,"z":3.168,"el":"Th"},{"x":7.142,"y":7.142,"z":3.168,"el":"Th"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.571,"z":4.752,"el":"Th"},{"x":7.142,"y":3.571,"z":4.752,"el":"Th"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.0,"z":6.336,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":7.142,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":7.142,"z":6.336,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.142,"y":0.0,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.142,"y":0.0,"z":6.336,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.142,"y":7.142,"z":0.0,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.142,"y":7.142,"z":6.336,"el":"Si"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.571,"z":1.584,"el":"Si"},{"x":7.142,"y":3.571,"z":1.584,"el":"Si"},{"x":1.26,"y":0.0,"z":1.046,"el":"O